      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "classified_as": [
        {
          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "a pot used as a unit of capacity — gallon, potle (two quarts), quart, pint, half-pint, usually of tin or pewter; also a pot as a measure for ginger, rose-water, conserva rosarum, confeccio, socate and similar wares, and (de virga) a yard of ale. See also pint pot, potelle."
    }
  ],
